WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.690
I saw on the news that there's
a new smartphone out,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:08.030
and people are lining
up at the shops to get it.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.360
That's weird, isn't it?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.820
It's a smartphone,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.410
but that isn't smart at all.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.660
They should be able
to put together some kind of

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.420
online reservation system
so you don't have to stand in line.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.560
But the fact that they didn't do that

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.310
means that the stores want lines!

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.360
They're deliberately making their
customers waste time standing in lines.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.160
Like, is it really worth it just
for the free advertising?

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.590
Those moments where you can just <i>tell</i> what
 somebody's thinking ruin everything.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:41.850
So?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.930
So I thought up an idea.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.710
A way to keep yourself in the news
while not making people stand in line.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.400
An amazing idea!

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.140
Get this...

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.790
You sell virtual tickets in virtual reality,

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.370
and make them stand in a virtual line!

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.210
Well, that was a waste of five minutes.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.810
I feel stupid for listening for that.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.810
The hell you say?

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.000
I want a new phone...

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.960
Once things calm down.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.550
Calm down?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.180
Oh, hey, girls!

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.580
What will you do when this battle is over?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.100
After we defeat the enemy Disas Beast!

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:25.560
<b>If This Battle Ever Ends</b>

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.700
Sacchuu's lucky.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.250
All he has to do is float in
the air while he eats junk food.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.950
He doesn't need to write reports.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.380
Chu!

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.000
I sent a report to the Spirit World's
Multidimensional Observation Army, chu!

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.460
I heard that fairy reports are just
a few paw prints on a piece of paper.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.910
That's racist, chu!

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.820
I mean, you're right, chu...

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.930
I am?

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.900
I'm gonna make some coffee, chu!

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.060
He ran.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.260
Lucky him.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.890
You're almost done.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:07.770
Hang in there.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.850
All work and no play makes Jack a dull boy.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.070
That's from a Kubrick film, isn't it?

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.950
The firepower a Magical Girl generates

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.530
isn't the kind of thing an individual
 would ordinarily be allowed to possess.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:26.400
And then there's the fact that magical
combat itself is an underdeveloped field.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.490
After action reports
are extremely important.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.000
I understand.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.290
Those reports are used
to analyze the enemy's forces,

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.640
and find their weak points.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.470
They save lives.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.490
I know that.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.000
I do...

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.560
But it's still exhausting, huh?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.330
It's a mental exhaustion,

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.430
not a physical one.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.450
I've got the perfect medicine for that!

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.040
It makes all that exhaustion just disappear.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:52.900
Stop it.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.580
You guys get less than most of us, you know.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.010
I'm done.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.610
I've got a lot to go.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.920
Should I help?

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.080
I'm fine.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.660
You can go home.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.730
I see...

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.130
Sorry.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.590
Resting when you can
is part of a soldier's job.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.530
Sorry for making you write the report.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.500
It's fine.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.920
They all look basically the same
no matter who writes them.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.150
Hey,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.060
that corpse that
was turned into a cube...

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.400
Dr. Greenburg.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.670
While you were fighting in Okinawa,

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:45.400
I went through all of his things,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.360
and his data that still remained in the cloud.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.860
Find anything?

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.720
No solid leads.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.760
But enough to form a hypothesis.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.960
Which is?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.460
He was being forced to calculate something.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.300
What is the Babel Brigade?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.390
They made him calculate something,

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.340
then started committing
terrorist acts all over the world

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.110
and gathering magic items.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:14.760
Magic is like physics in their world.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.080
It seems strange to us,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.540
but it has its rules and laws.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.800
If what Greenburg was calculating
was some kind of equation

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.460
involving the Disas and their world...

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.930
Some new way to commit terrorism,

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.920
or maybe summoning magic?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:33.410
It'd be nice to have 
more information, regardless.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.340
Okay, I'm heading to the hotel.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.300
I'll be there soon.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.790
That hotel...

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.920
It's got a glass-walled shower
room that's really naughty!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.310
Why do you say stuff like that?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:53.000
I was talking like Francine.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.370
You're going to torture me?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.740
Make it hurt.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.940
I'm used to it.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.250
Sorry.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.230
I don't think you know anything.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:19.800
But I need to torture you at least
once to be sure you're not lying.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.210
First,

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.280
a drug to sharpen your senses.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.760
I'll inject it directly into your brain.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.900
I told you in Okinawa
that I'd kill you, right?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.580
That was wrong.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:41.010
I let my feelings get the best of me.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.680
Your torture and pleasure
are about to begin.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.410
You may want to die.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.230
You may try to bite your tongue off,

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.030
or hang yourself.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:55.080
You may try lots of things.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.540
But I won't let you die.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.000
I'll heal any injuries you have.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.650
Hey,

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.760
have you ever seen the movie <i>Red Scorpion</i>?

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.730
I always replay the torture scene
from that movie over and over again.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.400
Well done, Tamara.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:26.140
Thank you.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.200
Your sister is happy as well.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.320
I have returned, Sister.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.100
I'm so happy...

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.210
that you'd say that about me.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.540
<b>Shanghai</b>

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.540
<i>Okay.</i>

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.920
<i>All the security cameras in the
area are under my control.</i>

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.570
The target for this job is in the back room
 on the restaurant's third floor.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:32.580
<i>Got it, my astrologer.</i>

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.570
<i>Once this is over,</i>

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.040
<i>I hope you and I can go have some fun!</i>

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:40.980
Your "fun" always ends up
being something involving sex.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.710
And you know you love it!

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.850
<i>Dummy!</i>

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:10.910
<i>Shuang Tou Long Peipei of the Magical Five.</i>

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.540
<i>Right now she uses the alias
"Liu Lang Zhe" in her job</i>

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.890
<i>as a freelance mercenary and assassin.</i>

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.840
Die for my wallet's sake!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:26.060
<b>Bangkok, Thailand</b>

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.450
This is what you used to look like, Peipei?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.030
I remember that old photo.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.380
You've changed a lot.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.170
I think I like your old hairstyle better.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:38.990
Aw...

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.450
I didn't change my face because I wanted to.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.610
I see.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.490
You've got a lot going on, huh?

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.170
Sorry.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.670
Everyone...

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.720
I brought a doggy.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.040
Woof! Woof!

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.620
When you make a naughty
girl see the error of her ways,

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.140
she can end up being pretty cute.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.910
Eventually, this little doggy
will help us in our fights.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.620
Fights?

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.700
Magical Girls are rare and precious.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.450
Without a certain level of latent magic,

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:35.090
you can't synchronize
properly with the fairies.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.860
There are about 30
Magical Girls in the world

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:42.480
designated as weapons by the 
UN Magical Security Council.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:48.080
But several terrorist groups
that use illegal Magical Girls,

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.410
like the Babel Brigade,
have been confirmed as well.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:55.780
Some speculate that there
may be over 300 of us out there.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.820
I see...

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:01.120
I'm one of those illegal
Magical Girls too, aren't I?

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.710
But 300 is the high-end estimate.

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:09.090
There are far fewer of them than
there are special forces or jet pilots.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.040
It would be a waste to 
completely break your mind here.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:14.920
Um...

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:15.840
Hmm?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.460
Aah! I'm sorry!

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.860
But there's something I want to tell her!

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.060
Well, fine.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.480
Um...

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:32.110
No matter what state you're in, 
I think it's important that you're alive.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.020
You can kinda see the shape I'm in now,

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.980
but this is my punishment
for doing bad things.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.030
And...

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:44.010
I feel a lot more relaxed now than 
I did when I belonged to a criminal gang.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:45.920
I...

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.850
I suffer so much just being alive.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.310
I thought I finally found hope, and...

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.330
It was fake.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.030
I can't go on!

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.090
Just kill me!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.850
I'm not going to kill you,

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:02.960
you stupid bitch.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:07.310
Even if you go through 99 painful things,

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.060
you can keep going as long
as there's one fun thing.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.660
You gather those things up,

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.240
and carry them with you throughout
your life like precious jewels.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.160
As long as you're alive,

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.220
the pain will continue.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.220
But in exchange,

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:25.290
there'll always be at least
one fun thing out there.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.060
I...

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.060
killed people.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.840
I hurt so many people.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:35.290
So you'll just have to save that
many lives, then, won't you?

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:41.690
Magical Girls don't die so easily.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.510
<i>This is such a happy ending, woof!</i>

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.470
You want Public Safety's Foreign Affairs
 section to help you?

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.520
Yes.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:09.800
The JSDF has groups that gather
information from overseas,

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:14.340
but the Foreign Affairs section has more
connections and has had far more past success.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:18.570
So you want Public Safety to cooperate 
unofficially with a JSDF special forces group.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.840
What's in it for us to justify the danger?

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.060
Commissioner Miura,

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:27.800
I understand your goal is to
establish a magical artillery platoon

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.270
within the Metropolitan Police
Special Assault Team unit.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:34.880
I have a suggestion as to who
you might want to hire.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.690
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:47.820
<i>That choker contains a magical drug.</i>

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.800
I'm letting you go,

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.940
but if you plan to escape or betray us,

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.090
the choker will pick it up immediately,

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.830
and give you such intense pain,
you won't be able to move.

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:00.590
Remember that.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.720
Liar.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.480
Let's go to a maid café!

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.620
Why?

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.730
We got that business card
from them during the festival!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.190
Maid Cafe
<b>Mitsuya</b>

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.400
<i>Those idiots.</i>

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:25.500
I'll make it clear before we start.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.220
This place is expensive and the food is bad.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:29.160
Well, we can't do anything
about it being bad,

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.860
but don't you think they'll give us
a discount 'cause they know us?

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.520
Maybe.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.930
Yeah.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:38.880
We've never paid, have we?

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.340
See?

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.820
We have to go, then!

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.700
They say nothing's more
expensive than free, you know.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.390
Welcome.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.280
You...

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.110
They're our new employees.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:57.230
Is that a good idea?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.070
Yeah.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.980
They say they've changed their ways.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:03.030
Thank you for what you did for me.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.650
What?

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.150
Did I do something?

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.300
Actually,

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.700
I was the one who referred them here.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.390
I feel like we've met.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.950
You're probably mistaken.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.650
I get that a lot.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:57.160
This really is bad.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.510
They said they could make it taste worse.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:01.410
Wow.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.620
I have no idea what that means!

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:06.590
Well, the ice was cold,
so I guess that's something!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.700
It would be hard for it to be anything else.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.690
It's really hot outside now.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:15.770
Actually...

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.560
Did you two get tans?

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.530
I don't know...

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:22.440
I've got delicate skin,

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.510
so even when we were in Okinawa,
 I put sunscreen on.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.730
Okinawa, huh?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.290
In Okinawa...

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.700
The Magical Girl you met in Okinawa...

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.630
What was she like?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.840
Well...

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:47.070
She was strong. Noble.

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.750
But she was still in pain.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:54.020
She was willing to put her life at risk
fighting for people she'd never met.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:57.850
And it wasn't just because
she was a Magical Girl.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.880
In our world,

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.230
there are always people like
that out there somewhere.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.410
People who can risk their lives
in battle for people they've never met.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.810
And I think that's the only reason
we can have something like peace,

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:16.520
or a normal life.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:22.740
I'm sorry for talking so much!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:23.960
No...

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.620
I'm sure if they heard that,

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:29.660
the Magical Girls would
say it was all worth it.

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:30.860
Yeah.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.710
My queen! My queen!

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.190
We've got all we need.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:22.600
Now all that's left is the vessel.

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:26.210
For an even greater war...

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.100
Abby,

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.520
do you know what you need for a war?

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.120
Umm...

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:35.480
Soldiers and weapons?

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:36.870
The answer is...

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.040
an enemy.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:41.490
Without an enemy, you can't start a war.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.890
And a big war needs a strong enemy.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:50.520
We need the Magical Girls
to get a little stronger.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:55.830
It's about time for summer break, huh?

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.470
And after that,

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.560
it's time to get ready for cultural festival.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.180
It's hard to believe we were ever at war.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.650
Sometimes it's the other way around.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:08.600
And it's hard to believe that
our daily life ever existed.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:09.960
Asuka-san...

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.930
What you said to me in the last battle...

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.210
That everyone who died would be mad.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.370
That hurt.

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:21.910
It felt like it woke me up.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.740
Thanks to Sayako and Nozomi,

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:30.580
I can finally understand what
it was that everybody protected.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.000
<i>The ones who died...</i>

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:57.840
<i>What they all protected
wasn't "peace" or "humanity,"</i>

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.840
<i>or anything big and important like that.</i>

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:02.140
<i>Having a normal life...</i>

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.140
<i>A tomorrow that always comes...</i>

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:07.960
<i>What really matters is keeping
the things we consider ordinary going.</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.230
This war might never end.

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.500
I'm sorry, Kurumi.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.250
I turned your life into something terrible.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.760
That's not...

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.220
Let's keep fighting forever.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.340
Wherever!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.850
<b>Iizuka-san
</b>Incoming Call

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:33.460
Yes.

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:44.690
Calm down?

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:46.860
Oh, hey, girls!

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:50.190
What will you do when this battle is over?

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.660
After we defeat the enemy Disas Beast!

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.690
You see scenes like that
in all the war movies.

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.240
The guys who talk about the
future are always the first to die.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:02.870
"When this battle's over,
I'm getting married!"

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.510
Something like that, chu!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.470
That's not what I meant.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.560
Who cares?

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.340
There's nothing wrong with tempting fate.

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:10.660
Francine...

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:13.190
Without a future, 
there's nothing worth fighting for.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.770
Yeah, that's true.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:19.250
Once the war's over, huh?

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.680
Well, there'll still be a
war going on somewhere,

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.780
so I'll be a soldier.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:25.180
Your father was a soldier too, right?

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:26.270
Yeah.

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:28.530
He died in a terrorist attack,
but I want to follow in his footsteps.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:31.550
I want to go back home and find success there.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:32.810
How, exactly?

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.570
I've fought for humanity's sake.

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:39.780
Now I want to fight
for money's sake. For money!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.850
I'm thinking of joining
a PLA Special Forces unit.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.480
Tamara, you're...

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:47.470
joining the Russian army, of course.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.400
Yes.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:49.550
A foolish question.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.890
What about you, Kurumi?

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:52.700
I...

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:56.400
When it's all over,

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.650
I'm thinking of falling in love, maybe?

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:02.520
No time like the present!

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:04.460
Let's lock ourselves in a room

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.930
and go at it like animals
for three days straight.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.490
I just bought lots of lube.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.420
If you keep talking like that,

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:14.240
I'll mess with your brain
and destroy your libido.

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:18.710
I wouldn't mind having a cute
girl operate on my brain.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.620
Well, you should.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.670
So what about you, Asuka?

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.010
I can't think about that now.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.470
I don't mind fighting,

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:32.920
but I don't know what I'll
do when the war's over.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:39.320
It feels like I don't have
anything left to do but fight.

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:46.890
Just keep trying things.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.150
People can change.

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:50.780
I'm sure you'll be fine.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.700
Here we go!

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:02.890
<i>Three years ago,</i>

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:07.720
<i>we defeated the leader of the enemies
that were trying to wipe out humanity.</i>

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:12.350
<i>Usually, that would be the happy ending.</i>

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:16.280
<i>But there are no endings in the real world.</i>

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:19.520
<i>Even after we defeated the last boss,</i>

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:22.200
<i>the world wasn't at peace.</i>

00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:25.400
<i>Our new battlefield is...</i>

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:28.030
<i>international crime,</i>

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:29.150
<i>terrorism,</i>

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:30.370
<i>civil war,</i>

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:31.880
<i>and other conflicts.</i>

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:36.920
<i>The battles of the Magical Girls...</i>

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:40.260
<i>will never end.</i>
